  "review_conclusions": [
    "The fixed10-byte prefix identifies wire encoding; the bounded body contains the ordered header and flat payload. Domain schema version and wire version have distinct ownership.",
    "Header decode lends the unparsed payload body after its prefix; loader schema/future-version checks occur before value interpretation, and full payload decoding rejects trailing bytes.",
    "The current-schema route constructs DeserializeOwned targets through the direct validated node adapter; older schema payloads become an owned JSON value before migration.",
    "The flat node stream uses preorder, explicit container cardinality and separate object-key nodes. Node capacity hints are capped; structural/domain checks remain explicit conversion responsibilities.",
    "JSON flattening reverses LIFO tasks to preserve key/value traversal; JSON reconstruction tracks pending object keys, remaining immediate values and a single root, and uses Entry to reject duplicate keys.",
    "Wire golden bytes lock header field order, positional options and all node discriminants. Existing malformed, migration, bool/enum/numeric-map and cross-format assertions were fully read and preserved.",
    "The ignored map benchmark measures map construction including result drop; it does not execute complete binary decoding. No runtime/performance result is claimed."
  ],
